<title>CANADA: CBRS upgrades Loblaw ratings, changes outlook.</title>
<headline>CBRS upgrades Loblaw ratings, changes outlook.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Bond Rating Service said it upgraded grocer Loblaw Cos Ltd's debentures and unsecured notes to A+ (Low) from A (High) and changed its rating outlook to stable.</p>
<p>CBRS reaffirmed Loblaw's commercial paper ratings at A-1, its preferred shares at P-2 (High) and its perpetual preferred shares at P-2.</p>
<p>&quot;The company is benefitting from strengthening margins and cash flow, (and) agressive capital expenditures,&quot; CBRS said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
</text>
